//api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.5d9a0ec4f46df7deb3c2c0e5015df58147db243f.001.1"},{"event":"Winter Storm Warning","headline":"Winter Storm Warning issued October 31 at 6:20PM MDT until November 2 at 11:00AM MST by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Heavy snow expected. Total snow accumulations 8 to 14\ninches. Winds gusting as high as 50 mph.\n\n* WHERE...Eastern San Juan Mountains Above 10000 Feet.\n\n* WHEN...From 5 PM Sunday to 11 AM MST Monday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Travel could be very difficult, especially Sunday night\nand Monday morning. Strong winds could produce areas of blowing and\ndrifting snow.","ends":"2026-11-02T11:00:00-07:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Eastern San Juan Mountains Above 10000 Ft","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.681963bb8119fe118c9c03d331c7709ba2bd3b05.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.681963bb8119fe118c9c03d331c7709ba2bd3b05.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued October 31 at 1:59PM MDT until November 2 at 11:00AM MST by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected to occur.\n\n* WHERE...A portion of south central Colorado, including the\nfollowing areas, the Eastern San Juan Mountains, and the Upper Rio\nGrande Valley.\n\n* WHEN...From late tonight through Monday morning.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone location.\nRockslides will be possible in the mountainous areas. Highway 160\nand Highway 17 will likely be significantly impacted by this storm.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Heavy rainfall is expected to fall Sunday and Monday across the\narea, leading to elevated concerns for flooding in areas that\nhave recently received excessive moisture, or have recently\nexperienced flooding.\n- The greatest risk of flooding will be along the Conejos River and\nthe South Fork of the Rio Grande, including South Fork and\nMogote.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-11-02T12:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Upper Rio Grande Valley/Eastern San Juan Mountains Below 10000 Ft; Eastern San Juan Mountains Above 10000 Ft","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a86d832769b4b479ba2fd2815cb3755bcf6b1d9a.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a86d832769b4b479ba2fd2815cb3755bcf6b1d9a.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-10-31T23:31:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 312331 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 531 PM MDT Sat Oct 31 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - High impact heavy precipitation/flooding event still on track for the eastern San Juans and portions of the San Luis Valley Sun/Mon, with flooding along the mainstem Rio Grande possible Mon-Wed. - Showers and isolated thunderstorms elsewhere over the mountains/val","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-10-31T23:01:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FLUS45 KPUB 312301 HWOPUB Hazardous Weather Outlook National Weather Service Pueblo CO 501 PM MDT Sat Oct 31 2026 COZ058>089-093>099-011300- Western Mosquito Range/East Lake County Above 11000 Feet- Leadville Vicinity/Lake County Below 11000 Feet- Eastern Sawatch Mountains Above 11000 Feet- Western Chaffee County Between 9000 and 11000 Feet- Central Chaffee County Below 9000 Feet- Western Mosq","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=HWO&format=CI"},"fwf":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-10-31T22:57:00+00:00","snippet":".Discussion... Critical fire weather conditions are not anticipated over the next 7 days. A strong weather system will bring heavy rainfall to the San Juan Mountains late tonight through Sunday night, with rain changing to heavy snow late Sunday night into Monday as snow levels fall. The San Juan Range and the San Luis Valley will be at elevated risk for flash flooding, especially from Sunday afte","url"